The council was furious. Citizens cursed her name. But physicians studying her honest patterns discovered the plague avoided certain water sources. They found the contamination. The truth, however harsh, showed the path to survival.

Her master had taught: pretty lies comfort briefly; ugly truths save permanently.

This is why weavers must sometimes create darkness before dawn—hope built on lies is no hope at all.

